WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.170
AI for 6G: a virtual live lab for next-generation wireless.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.940
Every experiment follows one path: four choices, one run, four readings, and a loop back.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:18.240
Three learning levels. The level sets what you are shown; it never locks anything away.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:26.040
The knowledge bank runs from the move from 3G to 6G, through reflecting surfaces, to deep joint source-channel coding.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:33.320
Six experiments. Each one is a question with an answer you can measure.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:48.920
Set the carrier, the geometry and the surface, then run it. Bit errors are counted over generated noise and plotted against the closed form. Aligned phases gain six decibels per doubling; random phases gain three.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:58.220
One scene, one channel, two systems. Both reconstructions are produced, then measured against the original.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:05.720
Three DeepJSCC architectures, trained offline, shipped with the held-out measurements that justify them.

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:14.500
And three datasets, generated by the same engine. Every result is reproducible from its configuration and seed.
